"""Verifier for the SLO credit closeout task.

Visible tier: the agent's /app/out (produced from /app/data) is compared with the reference close
through concept projections and through record slices: one per trap family, and one per decoy file
holding the records that change when that decoy's designated content is ignored. The per-source
reconciliation in data_quality.json is graded once, by concept_controls.

Hidden tier: the next month's exports are regenerated by the corpus generator embedded below as
plain source (its SHA-256 is pinned and checked before it runs), and the agent's own
/app/out/transform.py is run on them with the visible outputs as --prior. The transform is also run
on a copy of those exports with one support ticket removed, where the close must be HELD.

Agent code only ever runs as uid 65534 through setpriv, in its own session and under a timeout, and
every process of that uid is killed when a run ends. Everything it can read is root-owned and
read-only, and the generator is deleted before any agent code starts.
"""
